    "session_id": "cf674a50-a07b-45f0-8f90-fdacd716c322",
    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**. (The single `ERROR ExceptionControllerAdvice` line is an expected logged exception from a pre-existing `UserRestControllerV1Tests` negative-case test \u2014 its `Tests run: 5, Failures: 0` confirms it passed.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-match \"possible duplicate\" detection for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard (identityKey) duplicate but shares an existing owner's **last name** and **postcode** with a **different telephone**, it is still created and flagged.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These regenerate into `OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (`possible_duplicate` column) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`possible_duplicate_of` column), with getters/setters. They're stored so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns them (the acceptance test reads them back via a fresh GET).\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the two columns to the `owners` table. This matters because the test profile (`hsqldb`) uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema comes entirely from these files.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After the existing 409 hard-duplicate check, calls a new `applyPossibleDuplicate(owner)` helper that:\n   - Defaults `possibleDuplicate` to `false`.\n   - If the new owner has a postcode, scans existing owners for one sharing the last name (case-insensitive, collapsed whitespace via the existing `householdKey`) and exact postcode, but a different normalized (E.164) telephone.\n   - On a match, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the matching owner's id (lowest id when several match, for determinism).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the two same-named fields from `Owner` to `OwnerDto`, so no mapper changes were needed.",
